Preserve material identity and quality evidence through transfers, processing, and use (@metal-quality-handoffs: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @metals-and-metallurgical-production, #source "../sources/Aluminium-Automotive-Manual.lingua#r_73MPKA19MDBSQ96195B818Z49T", #source "../sources/Nonferrous-Metals-Industries-BREF.lingua#r_19ZD7KKDWVWM20MXVNCQZJMCDB", #source "../../../inquiry/metrology/Metrology.lingua#r_3G54ENPA974K19AB5XF0P641N5", #source "../sources/Metal-Recycling-UNEP-IRP.lingua#r_40JXFY43ST442BB8MJEAYJT9N1", #metals-and-metallurgical-production "Preserve-metallurgical-knowledge-and-distinguish-open-evidence-from-gaps.lingua#r_3ZXQYN51HZ74NR2HH24M5XGZQ5") { r_61D4D2RMGDTB681KWP8058BKR1
**Read:** [Aluminium Automotive Manual — European Aluminium and collaborators](../sources/Aluminium-Automotive-Manual.lingua#r_73MPKA19MDBSQ96195B818Z49T), complete product, manufacturing, joining, and functional-quality cases used; [Non-ferrous Metals Industries — European Commission BREF](../sources/Nonferrous-Metals-Industries-BREF.lingua#r_19ZD7KKDWVWM20MXVNCQZJMCDB), the full selected feed-to-product and quality account; [Measurement and metrology](../../../inquiry/metrology/Metrology.lingua#r_3G54ENPA974K19AB5XF0P641N5), reuse sampling, uncertainty, reference systems, comparison, and conformity evidence; [Metal Recycling: Opportunities, Limits, Infrastructure — UNEP International Resource Panel](../sources/Metal-Recycling-UNEP-IRP.lingua#r_40JXFY43ST442BB8MJEAYJT9N1), the complete product-to-material recovery context.

Feed lots, melts/heats, castings, rolled or forged product, heat-treatment batches, joined assemblies, samples, returns, and recovered material have related but different identities. Mixing, splitting, reactions, deformation, treatment, repairs, and service change the physical population and the meaning of a test result.

Trace actual provenance, quantities, location/orientation, history, samples/methods, calibration, specification/standard editions, uncertainty, deviations, and decisions. A certificate, digital label, or database entry is evidence only for what it actually identifies and supports. It does not eliminate a missing sample, changed material state, unobserved defect, or incompatible test basis.

Transfers include knowledge and responsibility as well as physical material. Explain who measured what, which observations were accepted, what remains disputed, and what the receiving process requires. Preserve competing results and the original basis rather than rewriting historical evidence to match a final quality label.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete material/evidence chain from feed to a specified product, a service/repair change, and recovery. Independently reconcile an important quantity/impurity and test-support transition. Investigate a quality disagreement using original methods and material history, then propose the observation that could resolve it. Explain how another party can verify the transferred claim and continue the required processing, inspection, maintenance, or recovery work.

**Continue:** [Keep metallurgical knowledge reconstructable through sources, methods, versions, and challenges](Preserve-metallurgical-knowledge-and-distinguish-open-evidence-from-gaps.lingua#r_3ZXQYN51HZ74NR2HH24M5XGZQ5).

